  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_010 (multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the current best at 0.639 acc / 10.60 GPU hrs, clearly showing that multiprofile + avgpool + weighted fusion is the strongest combination. The two untested levers that could push accuracy higher are the RNA encoder (PCA is linear and limited) and the image encoder (ResNet50 is mid-tier). This experiment tests upgrading the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings at their proven best (multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool, weighted), giving a clean single-variable ablation. It clarifies whether the image representation is a bottleneck: if accuracy improves meaningfully over 0.639, the visual pathway is under-utilized and further gains may come from pairing ViT-L with a learned RNA encoder; if it does not, the RNA encoder is the priority. Expected cost: ViT-L is roughly 2× the parameters of ResNet50, so I estimate ~15–20 GPU hrs—moderately more expensive than config_010 but well within budget, and cheaper than the concat-fusion runs (~36 GPU hrs). With 5 experiments remaining, this focused test is the highest-information-per-cost choice before committing to a full dual-encoder upgrade."
}

